Q: Undefined symbols for architecture arm64: &quot;_kfun:androidx.lifecycle.viewmodel.compose A: <p>Looking for a solution I tried many things like <code>kotlin.native.cacheKind=none</code>, but they didn't work.</p>
<p>In my case I have KMP project where I added <code>ViewModel</code>s with parameters. While it worked in Android, it wasn't built in xCode. After some fixes (<code>build.gradle</code> and <code>libs.version.toml</code>) it compiled, but after running on iPhone it crashed in some screens (that inject <code>ViewModel</code>with parameters).</p>
<p>The main upgrade you should do is upgrade several <code>Koin</code>libraries to at least <code>4.1.0</code> or newer to support iOS architecture.</p>
<pre><code>io.insert-koin:koin-android:4.1.0
io.insert-koin:koin-core:4.1.0
io.insert-koin:koin-androidx-compose:4.1.0
io.insert-koin:koin-compose-viewmodel:4.1.0
io.insert-koin:koin-core-viewmodel:4.1.0
io.insert-koin:koin-test:4.1.0
</code></pre>
<p>You should add them to various <code>dependencies</code> blocks:</p>
<pre><code>sourceSets {
    androidMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.koin.android)
        implementation(libs.koin.core)
    }
    commonMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.koin.core)
        implementation(libs.koin.compose)
        // Koin viewModel
        implementation(libs.koin.core.viewmodel) // Core KMP support
        implementation(libs.koin.compose.viewmodel) // For Compose integration
    }
    iosMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.koin.core)
    }
    commonTest.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.koin.test)
    }

    // Not sure but also:
    all {
        languageSettings {
            optIn(&quot;kotlin.experimental.ExperimentalObjCName&quot;)
            optIn(&quot;kotlin.time.ExperimentalTime&quot;)
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Google advises to add this to resolve <code>import androidx.lifecycle.compose.collectAsStateWithLifecycle</code>:</p>
<pre><code>// build.gradle.kts (commonMain)
sourceSets {
    commonMain.dependencies {
        // Use the Jetbrains/Google KMP version (usually 2.8.0 or higher)
        implementation(&quot;org.jetbrains.androidx.lifecycle:lifecycle-runtime-compose:2.8.0&quot;) 
        // OR the standard Google KMP-enabled version
        implementation(&quot;androidx.lifecycle:lifecycle-runtime-compose:2.8.0&quot;)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>See also <a href="https://dev.to/saad4software/kmp-native-ui-view-model-injection-for-ios-and-android-2nc1" rel="nofollow noreferrer">link</a> for additional <code>plugins</code> support in iOS.</p>
<p>Then you can inject <code>ViewModel</code>s so:</p>
<pre><code>val viewModelModule = module {
    viewModelOf(::MapScreenViewModel)
    // Or
    viewModel { (latitude: Double, longitude: Double, city: String) -&gt;
        MapScreenViewModel(
            latitude = latitude,
            longitude = longitude,
            city = city,
        )
    }
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>import org.koin.compose.koinInject
import org.koin.compose.viewmodel.koinViewModel
import org.koin.core.parameter.parametersOf

@Composable
fun MapScreen() {
    val viewModel: MapScreenViewModel = koinViewModel(
        parameters = { parametersOf(latitude, longitude, city) }
    )
}
</code></pre>
